  "answer": "All five writable files were rewritten; no other files were touched.\n\n**What changed**\n\n- `normalize.mjs` — `normalizeIssue` no longer mutates the input. It validates via the existing `assertIssue` (which already throws `TypeError('invalid issue')` for the contract violations), then builds a fresh object in property order `id, title, tags, assignee`: ID/title trimmed with case preserved, tags trimmed + `toLowerCase()` + empty-dropped + first-occurrence de-duplicated into a new array, assignee trimmed/lowercased with empty → `null` and input `null` preserved. Frozen inputs work since nothing is written.\n- `consumers/list.mjs` — removed the `sort` (which also mutated the caller's array) and the `map(normalizeIssue)` callback that passed index/array args; now a plain `issues.map(issue => normalizeIssue(issue))`, preserving input order and duplicate IDs, returning a fresh array.\n- `consumers/search.mjs` — validates `query` as a string, builds the normalized list once, trims/lowercases the query, returns the whole list for an empty query, and matches on normalized title (case-insensitive) or any normalized tag. No ID/assignee matching; no shared output array.\n- `consumers/activity.mjs` — now goes through `listIssues` (so validation and normalization apply), renders `null` assignee as `-`, joins tags with commas, and returns a fresh string array.\n- `serialize.mjs` — serializes `listIssues(issues)` instead of raw input, so order, property order, and extra-field stripping match the list view.\n\n`legacy.mjs`, `api.mjs`, `validators.mjs`, fixtures, and the date/paging/console helpers were left untouched, so `legacyTitle`, `boardSnapshot` key order, and neighboring behavior are unchanged.\n\n**What was checked:** I re-read the final `serialize.mjs` and reviewed each edit against the spec by inspection. No tests were executed — there is no shell/test runner available in this environment, so `public.test.mjs` was not run.",
